    <div class="fa-wrap fa-hero-inner">
      <span class="fa-eyebrow">About Fayetteville Fury</span>
      <h1 class="fa-title">A club built around <span class="fa-title-accent">the player.</span></h1>
      <div class="fa-copy"><p>Fayetteville Fury is a youth soccer club focused on player development and tournament competition for boys and girls through high school.</p></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="fa-who" aria-labelledby="fa-who-title">
    <div class="fa-wrap fa-split">
      <div>
        <span class="fa-eyebrow">Who We Are</span>
        <h2 class="fa-heading" id="fa-who-title">Development with <span class="fa-heading-accent">direction.</span></h2>
        <div class="fa-identity-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fa-copy">
        <p>Fury puts individual growth at the center of the game. Our current identity is built on player development, purposeful tournament competition, and preparing players for whatever comes next.</p>
        <p>We serve young players through high school in a supportive club community where training has a purpose, competition provides feedback, and progress matters.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fa-why" aria-label="Why Fayetteville Fury exists">
    <div class="fa-wrap">
      <blockquote>Fayetteville Fury exists because every young player deserves the opportunity to grow, be challenged, and discover how far their passion for soccer can take them.</blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fa-purpose" aria-label="Mission and vision">
    <div class="fa-wrap fa-purpose-grid">
      <article class="fa-purpose-card">
        <span class="fa-eyebrow">Our Mission</span>
        <h2 class="fa-card-title">Purpose in every step.</h2>
        <p>To develop youth soccer players through purposeful training, challenging tournament competition, and a supportive club community. Fayetteville Fury puts individual growth at the center of the game, helping players build technical ability, soccer intelligence, confidence, and character while preparing them for their next challenge on and off the field.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="fa-purpose-card">
        <span class="fa-eyebrow">Our Vision</span>
        <h2 class="fa-card-title">Progress defines success.</h2>
        <p>To build a soccer community where boys and girls can grow from developing players into confident competitors and leaders. We aspire to make Fayetteville Fury a model for youth development, where progress defines success, competition inspires growth, and a lifelong love of the game connects players, families, and our community.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fa-model" aria-labelledby="fa-model-title">
    <div class="fa-wrap">
      <div class="fa-model-head">
        <div><span class="fa-eyebrow">The Fury Model</span><h2 class="fa-heading" id="fa-model-title">A cycle built for <span class="fa-heading-accent">growth.</span></h2></div>
        <div class="fa-copy"><p>Each stage supports the next. Coaches and players train with intention, test progress in meaningful competition, and use what they learn to keep moving forward.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fa-steps">
        <article class="fa-step" data-step="01"><h3 class="fa-step-title">Train</h3><p>Build skills and habits through purposeful work.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-step" data-step="02"><h3 class="fa-step-title">Develop</h3><p>Turn instruction and repetition into individual growth.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-step" data-step="03"><h3 class="fa-step-title">Compete</h3><p>Use selected tournaments to test development.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-step" data-step="04"><h3 class="fa-step-title">Advance</h3><p>Prepare for the next opportunity, whatever it may be.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fa-difference" aria-labelledby="fa-difference-title">
    <div class="fa-wrap">
      <div class="fa-difference-head"><span class="fa-eyebrow">What Makes Fury Different</span><h2 class="fa-heading" id="fa-difference-title">The player is the <span class="fa-heading-accent">priority.</span></h2></div>
      <div class="fa-difference-grid">
        <article class="fa-card"><span class="fa-card-number">01</span><h3 class="fa-card-title">Player-First Development</h3><p>We focus on the individual player rather than treating the team scoreline as the only measure of success. Where appropriate, smaller player-to-coach ratios give coaches more time to help individual players develop.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-card"><span class="fa-card-number">02</span><h3 class="fa-card-title">Purposeful Competition</h3><p>Players do not need to travel every weekend simply for the sake of competition. Our rhythm is train, develop, compete, improve—using tournaments to test focused work.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-card"><span class="fa-card-number">03</span><h3 class="fa-card-title">Success Is More Than the Score</h3><p>A win matters, but it does not tell the whole story. We measure physical, technical, tactical, mental, and personal growth. Competition is feedback.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-card"><span class="fa-card-number">04</span><h3 class="fa-card-title">Accessible Development</h3><p>We work to provide meaningful development while keeping costs accessible. Financial assistance may be available to qualifying families based on financial need and available scholarship funding.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-card"><span class="fa-card-number">05</span><h3 class="fa-card-title">Preparing Players for What Comes Next</h3><p>That next step may be high school, college, a national team or professional opportunity, another level of competition, or simply continued growth as a player and person.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fa-programs" aria-labelledby="fa-programs-title">
    <div class="fa-wrap">
      <div class="fa-programs-head">
        <div><span class="fa-eyebrow">Our Programs</span><h2 class="fa-heading" id="fa-programs-title">A place to <span class="fa-heading-accent">progress.</span></h2></div>
        <div class="fa-copy"><p>Fury NXT is our current travel and tournament youth program and an important part of the club's player-development model.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fa-program-grid">
        <article class="fa-program-card"><span class="fa-age">8U · 10U · 12U · 14U</span><p>These age groups currently play during both fall and spring, with a winter break.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-program-card"><span class="fa-age">16U · 18U · 19U Boys</span><p>These boys' teams currently play in the fall.</p></article>
        <article class="fa-program-card"><span class="fa-age">Girls Programming</span><p>Fury is actively working toward fielding 16U, 18U, and 19U girls teams and expanding girls programming across the other age groups.</p></article>
      </div>
