  <section class="fa-advance" aria-labelledby="fa-advance-title">
    <div class="fa-wrap fa-advance-grid">
      <div><span class="fa-eyebrow">Advance</span><h2 class="fa-heading" id="fa-advance-title">Prepare for whatever comes <span class="fa-heading-accent">next.</span></h2><span class="fa-advance-tag">The Fury Pathway</span></div>
      <div class="fa-advance-copy">
        <p>Fury players have gone on to national team opportunities, college soccer, and professional soccer opportunities in Germany, Canada, and Australia. These paths show what preparation can make possible; they are not a promise that every player will reach the same destination.</p>
        <p>The 2025–2026 season marks Fury's first high school graduating class. Fury is no longer only developing young players—the club is now seeing players reach the point where preparation for the next stage becomes a central responsibility.</p>
        <p>From freshman through senior year, Fury helps high school players understand college recruitment, build player profiles, use platforms such as FieldLevel, create recruiting video, use Trace resources, market themselves, contact college coaches, and present themselves to higher levels of competition. The goal is to provide these resources at the lowest practical cost possible.</p>
        <ul class="fa-advance-list"><li>High school soccer</li><li>College soccer</li><li>National team opportunities</li><li>Professional opportunities</li><li>Another level of competition</li><li>Growth as a player and person</li></ul>
        <p class="fa-advance-quote">Fury prepares the player for the next opportunity. The destination may be different for every player.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

